doc.para:
Math.RandomGenerator Class Math.RandomGenerator is a class for generating random numbers using the Mersenne Twister method. The syntax for the constructor is as follows:
new Math.RandomGenerator([<seed>]);
If a numerical value is specified in the constructor, the random number generator is initialized with that value. If a dictionary array object whose state was saved using the serialize method is specified in the constructor, the random number generator will be created with that state. If the constructor argument is omitted, the random number generator is initialized with a random value based on the current time (in Kirikiri 2, it is initialized with a random number from a generator based on environmental noise, rather than the current time).
